      {
        "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n\n    // A flat byte array avoids the per-row allocations and proxy-bit accesses\n    // of vector<vector<bool>> while retaining O(N^2) storage.\n    vector<unsigned char> blockedCells(static_cast<size_t>(n) * n, 0);\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; c++) {\n        int i, j;\n        cin >> i >> j;\n        blockedCells[static_cast<size_t>(i) * n + j] = 1;\n    }\n\n    // The row recurrence needs only the previous row and the current row's\n    // left neighbor, so a single rolling array is sufficient.\n    vector<int> dp(n, 0);\n    if (!blockedCells[0])\n        dp[0] = 1;\n\n    for (int j = 1; j < n; j++) {\n        if (blockedCells[j])\n            dp[j] = 0;\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n        const size_t row = static_cast<size_t>(i) * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            if (blockedCells[row + j]) {\n                dp[j] = 0;\n            } else if (j != 0) {\n                dp[j] += dp[j - 1];\n                if (dp[j] >= MOD)\n                    dp[j] -= MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\n';\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "The row-wise dynamic-programming recurrence has a loop-carried dependency through dp[j-1], so straightforward OpenMP work sharing would either change the result or add synchronization overhead that outweighs any benefit. This experiment keeps the correct sequential recurrence as a control rather than introducing unsafe parallelism.",
